  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:89860",
  "description": "The httpd packages provide the Apache HTTP Server, a powerful, efficient, and extensible web server.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * httpd: httpd: HTTP response smuggling via crafted Transfer-Encoding response in mod_proxy_uwsgi (CVE-2026-63718)\n  * httpd: httpd: Denial of Service via integer overflow in mod_dav_fs (CVE-2026-93546)\n  * httpd: httpd: Authentication state corruption via concurrent Digest authentication requests (CVE-2026-73637)\n  * httpd: httpd: unauthorized connection to arbitrary hosts via crafted FTP PASV response (CVE-2026-63045)\n  * httpd: httpd: Arbitrary code execution via oversized Host header in mod_vhost_alias (CVE-2026-63292)\n  * httpd: httpd: mod_heartmonitor: Denial of Service via NULL pointer dereference (CVE-2026-46729)\n  * httpd: httpd: Authentication bypass via credential replay in mod_auth_digest (CVE-2026-73636)\n  * httpd: httpd: Denial of Service via charset conversion failure in mod_xml2enc (CVE-2026-63686)\n  * httpd: httpd: Denial of service via forged Authorization headers in mod_auth_digest (CVE-2026-48005)\n  * httpd: httpd: Denial of Service via mod_rewrite lookahead (CVE-2026-56154)\n  * httpd: httpd: Denial of Service via heap-based buffer overflow in mod_charset_lite (CVE-2026-56153)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
  "fromstr": "packager@almalinux.org",
